{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>Therefore.</b> Since in this first one the blessed El intended that she be like the man as much as possible, so that He formed her from his body." "<b>A man shall leave his father and his mother and cling to his wife.</b> It is fitting that a person endeavor to take a wife suitable for him and worthy of clinging to him, even though he must leave his father and his mother — for there is no true clinging between dissimilar persons, but only between similar ones, for then they direct themselves to a single mind." "<b>And they shall become one flesh.</b> Directed in all their actions toward attaining the perfection intended in the creation of man, as though the two of them existed as one alone."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:28:46.139004240Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}